issue_context.body:
I found 2 suspicious code fragments with possible incorrect order of arguments. 

The `XmlConfigurationElementTextContent` constructor signature:
```csharp
public XmlConfigurationElementTextContent(string textContent, int? linePosition, int? lineNumber)
```
[Link to the sources](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/v7.0.0/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Xml/src/XmlConfigurationElementTextContent.cs)

The second argument is `linePosition` and the third is `lineNumber`. 
It looks like in both cases below the `lineNumber` and the `linePosition` arguments are mixed up. 

**Suspicious call №1**
```csharp
if (preNodeType == XmlNodeType.Element)
{
  var lineInfo = reader as IXmlLineInfo;
  var lineNumber = lineInfo?.LineNumber;
  var linePosition = lineInfo?.LinePosition;
  parent.TextContent = new XmlConfigurationElementTextContent(string.Empty, lineNumber, linePosition);
 }
```
[Link to the sources](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/d099f075e45d2aa6007a22b71b45a08758559f80/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Xml/src/XmlStreamConfigurationProvider.cs#L133)

**Suspicious call №2**
```csharp
if (currentPath.Count != 0)
{
  var lineInfo = reader as IXmlLineInfo;
  var lineNumber = lineInfo?.LineNumber;
  var linePosition = lineInfo?.LinePosition;

  XmlConfigurationElement parent = currentPath.Peek();

  parent.TextContent = new XmlConfigurationElementTextContent(reader.Value, lineNumber, linePosition);
}
```
[Link to the sources](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/d099f075e45d2aa6007a22b71b45a08758559f80/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Xml/src/XmlStreamConfigurationProvider.cs#L148)
